# License

This repository is mixed-licensed: each directory carries the license of the upstream
project it ports, so different parts of the tree are under different terms.

## MIT

Applies to `crates/maho-*`, `crates/builtins`, `crates/extensions`, `crates/vendor`,
and every other file not listed under SUL-1.0 below. These port
[senpi](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi) (MIT).
Full text: `LICENSES/MIT.txt`

## Sustainable Use License 1.0 (SUL-1.0)

Applies to `crates/omo/**`, which ports
[oh-my-openagent](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent).
Also applies to the `maho-cli` source files compiled only with its `omo` cargo feature
(`#[cfg(feature = "omo")]` modules in `crates/maho-cli/src/cli/mod.rs` and
`crates/maho-cli/src/lib.rs`), which port the host side of oh-my-openagent.
Full text: `LICENSES/SUL-1.0.md`

The SUL-1.0 portions may be used, copied, modified, and used to prepare derivative works
for your own internal business purposes or for non-commercial or personal use. They may be
distributed or provided to others only free of charge for non-commercial purposes. All
licensing, copyright, or other notices of the licensor must be preserved.

## Distributed binaries

The shipped `mhc` executable links SUL-1.0 code, so its distribution is governed by
SUL-1.0 as well as MIT. Distribution of the combined binary is permitted only free of
charge for non-commercial purposes, and all notices must be preserved.

